import java.io.File;

public class FileCounter {
    public int countFilesWithExtension(String directoryPath, String fileExtension) {
        File directory = new File(directoryPath);
        if (!directory.exists() || !directory.isDirectory()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid directory path");
        }
        return countFilesWithExtensionInDirectory(directory, fileExtension);
    }

    private int countFilesWithExtensionInDirectory(File directory, String fileExtension) {
        int count = 0;
        File[] files = directory.listFiles();
        if (files != null) {
            for (File file : files) {
                if (file.isDirectory()) {
                    count += countFilesWithExtensionInDirectory(file, fileExtension);
                } else if (file.getName().endsWith("." + fileExtension)) {
                    count++;
                }
            }
        }
        return count;
    }
}
```

The `countFilesWithExtension` method takes the directory path and file extension as input and returns the count of files with the specified extension. It first validates the directory path and then calls the `countFilesWithExtensionInDirectory` method to recursively count the files with the given extension in the directory and its subdirectories. The `countFilesWithExtensionInDirectory` method recursively traverses the directory structure and counts the files with the specified extension.

